CC0 1.0 Universal

Statement of Purpose

The laws of most jurisdictions throughout the world automatically confer
exclusive Copyright and Related Rights (defined below) upon the creator and
subsequent owner(s) (each and all, "rightful owners") of an original work of
authorship and/or a database (each, a "Work").

Certain owners wish to permanently relinquish those rights to a Work for the
purpose of contributing to a commons, an effort to rebuild a shared body of
creative and cultural works, an ecosystem of freely available information,
and public infrastructure.

To the greatest extent permitted by, but not in contravention of, applicable
law, each rightful owner hereby waives, and covenants not to assert,
certain rights related to a Work, as set forth below.

1. Copyright and Related Rights.
   A Work made available under CC0 may be protected by copyright and related
   or neighboring rights ("Copyright and Related Rights"). Copyright and
   Related Rights include, but are not limited to, the following:

     i. the right to reproduce, adapt, distribute, perform, display,
        communicate, and translate a Work;
    ii. moral rights retained by the original author(s) and/or performer(s);
   iii. publicity and privacy rights pertaining to a person's image or
        likeness depicted in a Work;
    iv. rights protecting against unfair competition in regards to a Work,
        subject to the limitations in paragraph 4, below;
     v. rights protecting the extraction, dissemination, use and reuse of
        data in a Work;
    vi. database rights (such as those arising under Section 2 of the
        Database Rights and Regulations, and any successor legislation);

2. Waiver.
   To the greatest extent permitted by, but not in contravention of,
   applicable law, each rightful owner hereby waives all of the Copyright
   and Related Rights in the Work, and covenants not to assert such rights
   against any person who makes use of the Work ("You"), whether by
   assertion of the rights, by bringing suit, or otherwise.

3. Public License Fallback.
   Should any part of the above waiver be held invalid or unenforceable
   under applicable law, the applicable license is hereby granted,
   free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of the Work, to use,
   copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell
   copies of the Work, and to permit persons to whom the Work is
   furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:

     The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be
     included in all copies or substantial portions of the Work.

4. Limitations.
   In no event and under no legal theory shall any rightful owner be
   liable to You for damages arising out of the use of the Work, and
   the Work is provided "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND.

   This waiver does not affect: (a) patent or trademark rights of any
   rightful owner; (b) rights of other persons to the Work itself;
   (c) uses of the Work that may be permitted by applicable law or
   fair use; or (d) moral rights of authors, where waiving them is
   not permitted by law.

For the full legal code, see:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
